{:edb/db-before-t 2384 :edb/db-after-t 2385 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535697 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:28:12.675Z" 13194139535697 true] [17592186068786 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361834 13194139535697 true] [17592186087672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361871 13194139535697 true] [17592186087697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361855 13194139535697 true] [17592186100787 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361864 13194139535697 true] [17592186157260 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361848 13194139535697 true] [17592186175827 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361841 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361835 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1089 "q-123278" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1100 "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t-3⟩,$ $|r(6)|=$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1113 #uuid "0a8aedd2-1097-5d66-8eeb-656de3e77ac4" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361834 1145 "Evaluating the function at $t=6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(6) & =⟨\\sqrt{6+1},\\,6-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{7},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(6)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{7})}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7+9} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361836 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361837 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361838 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361839 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361840 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1041 "selection" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361840 13194139535697 true] [17592186361835 1110 #uuid "6d8c70c9-1f61-531a-a728-132ab42cd996" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361836 1034 "\\sqrt{10}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361836 1111 #uuid "f3e11121-d75e-58b3-9ea2-ba2fb56b4903" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361837 1034 "\\sqrt{7}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361837 1111 #uuid "96a25913-19bf-5520-8ebc-f479e0acec17" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361838 1034 "7" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361838 1111 #uuid "8d62874a-e38d-52cd-b6c1-92ca38cbebd8" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361839 1034 "2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361839 1111 #uuid "ee41d749-511b-5c6d-8e88-2d96994657f7" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361840 1034 "4" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361840 1111 #uuid "556f2eaa-8d04-56cc-ad3e-a0ef176f8198" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361842 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1089 "q-129219" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1100 "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}?$ \n\n- $(-2,2]$\n- $[-2,4]$\n- $(-2,4)$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1113 #uuid "ca1b55ce-6618-59da-a758-cf727ab94fd4" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361841 1145 "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $(-2,2]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,4)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361843 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361844 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361845 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361846 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361847 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1041 "selection" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361847 13194139535697 true] [17592186361842 1110 #uuid "5269d4ef-ca3d-5fc7-8098-eda91769c803" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361843 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535697 true] [17592186361843 1111 #uuid "7fc4b4cb-9e3d-52a5-b4e0-bf340402c95f" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361844 1034 "I only" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535697 true] [17592186361844 1111 #uuid "5ce2dd99-f10b-52b0-be9f-6b42aa560d9a" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361845 1034 "III only" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535697 true] [17592186361845 1111 #uuid "4a2b73ff-75e0-58d5-b280-bca31579eaa6" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361846 1034 "None" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535697 true] [17592186361846 1111 #uuid "fd1970cb-22e3-5928-b7b7-06ef9ca9a93c" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361847 1034 "II only" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535697 true] [17592186361847 1111 #uuid "d8547ab0-a3ca-54f8-b924-8ef28c4e00a2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361849 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361851 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361853 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1089 "q-276950" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)+1\\le \\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9).$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\le \\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1113 #uuid "30a43708-f16f-596d-8fb5-c42ef7a03f99" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361848 1145 "We use each side of the inequality as an exponent of $10.$ This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)+1} & \\le {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9)} \\\\ {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2-x)}\\cdot {10}^{1} & \\le {10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+9)} \\\\ (2-x)\\cdot 10 & \\le x+9 \\\\ 20-10x & \\le x+9 \\\\ -11x & \\le -11 \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the logarithms in the original inequality. To find the domain of the logarithms, we recall that the argument of the logarithm must be positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & <2 \\\\ x+9 & >0 & ⇒ &  & x & >-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x\\ge 1,$ which can be expressed as $[1,\\infty ).$ Additionally, the domains of the logarithms are $x<2$ and $x>-11,$ which can be expressed as $(-\\infty ,2)$ and $(-11,\\infty )$ respectively. To find the solutions that are in the domains of the logarithms, we take the intersection:\n\n$$\n[1,\\infty )\\cap (-\\infty ,2)\\cap (-9,\\infty )=[1,2)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [1,2),$ which can also be written as $1\\le x<2.$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361850 13194139535697 true] [17592186361849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361849 1041 "field-1" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361850 13194139535697 true] [17592186361849 1110 #uuid "0bb8d367-be22-5532-b11b-b266c6ffd1d9" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361850 1034 "1" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361850 1111 #uuid "6ad18234-c2f1-5de7-8b86-0489a830a837" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361851 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361852 13194139535697 true] [17592186361851 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361851 1041 "field-2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361851 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361852 13194139535697 true] [17592186361851 1110 #uuid "f01ef642-7656-5c8c-af96-d141a5faa304" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361852 1034 "<" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361852 1111 #uuid "e0717a19-164f-51e4-8032-7b3d3f142c0d" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361853 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361854 13194139535697 true] [17592186361853 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361853 1041 "field-3" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361853 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361854 13194139535697 true] [17592186361853 1110 #uuid "ac5f18b9-9ac7-5341-94e3-123cfdb29d0f" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361854 1034 "2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361854 1111 #uuid "07676991-05b9-5258-a67e-8d3deef9d373" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361856 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361858 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361860 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361862 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1089 "q-316656" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1100 "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1113 #uuid "ffd0c8c4-243f-527a-8c14-0416289f3f43" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361855 1145 "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -4(x-5)({x}^{2}+2x+5) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x-5{x}^{2}-10x-25) & = \\\\ -4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5x-25) & = \\\\ -4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-4{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+20x+100.$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361857 13194139535697 true] [17592186361856 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361856 1041 "field-1" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361856 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361857 13194139535697 true] [17592186361856 1110 #uuid "caacf1bc-fd87-52e7-a970-e14f936e68d2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361857 1034 "-4" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361857 1111 #uuid "1e783eb9-a681-5eba-aacc-969cf4aaad76" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361859 13194139535697 true] [17592186361858 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361858 1041 "field-2" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361858 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361859 13194139535697 true] [17592186361858 1110 #uuid "6e87432d-f293-5f0a-97cd-73a0d11f52b5" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361859 1034 "12" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361859 1111 #uuid "61eee858-9a01-5916-a798-6dae9f065b3b" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361861 13194139535697 true] [17592186361860 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361860 1041 "field-3" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361860 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361861 13194139535697 true] [17592186361860 1110 #uuid "28148e31-6f17-509e-82a6-3b63ae1ce93d" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361861 1034 "20" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361861 1111 #uuid "0db6309b-88a7-5654-a2cc-a9af8a9e88e9" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361863 13194139535697 true] [17592186361862 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535697 true] [17592186361862 1041 "field-4" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361862 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361863 13194139535697 true] [17592186361862 1110 #uuid "e1338656-9fbd-550f-a4c6-448c80dd2aec" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361863 1034 "100" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361863 1111 #uuid "c5cc0e13-1cd7-5e8d-b698-eb812c0cbabe" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361865 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1089 "q-49613" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1100 "Evaluate the definite integral ${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(5x-6)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1113 #uuid "b67dc0a6-51f8-5dfe-a448-7ac0ef9d5e96" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361864 1145 "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =5x-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =5\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5x-6.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ u & 4 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\sqrt{{(5x-6)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{4}^{9}{u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}({9}^{5/2}-{4}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}(({3}^{2})^{5/2}-({2}^{2})^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}({3}^{5}-{2}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{25}(243-32) \\\\  & =\\frac{422}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361866 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361867 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361868 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361869 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361870 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1041 "selection" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361870 13194139535697 true] [17592186361865 1110 #uuid "a058c696-13e3-591e-a553-6de7c76888cd" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361866 1034 "\\frac{484}{25}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361866 1111 #uuid "36ab5a53-ee6a-55d4-891a-4100dfe7b2f8" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361867 1034 "\\frac{211}{5}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361867 1111 #uuid "ef99a009-6ed9-516b-9f51-a639fc401277" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361868 1034 "\\frac{96}{5}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361868 1111 #uuid "28f896fe-615c-5693-99e7-b6591110f4c5" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361869 1034 "\\frac{2}{25}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361869 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361869 1111 #uuid "f4b80bb4-7776-5793-95cb-0a1dff265265" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361870 1034 "\\frac{422}{25}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361870 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361870 1111 #uuid "2f124855-4137-5692-a3f2-69212423fd83" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361872 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1089 "q-71979" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1100 "Write the complex number $z=3-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}$ in exponential form." 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1113 #uuid "ce405741-9ecc-5ff1-a4c2-a25ead99ec54" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1142 true 13194139535697 true] [17592186361871 1145 "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361873 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361874 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361875 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361876 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361877 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1041 "selection" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361877 13194139535697 true] [17592186361872 1110 #uuid "313e1229-1616-5b11-a259-8de3d7c72c67" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361873 1034 "z=4\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{11\\pi \\text{i}/6}" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535697 true] [17592186361873 1111 #uuid "da77c455-02e5-50bd-810e-e340a636b71c" 13194139535697 true] [17592186361874 1034 "z=4\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}" 131